          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1.6 Relation to Number Sequences"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.345,
            0.835,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Often, shape sequences are related to number sequences in surprising ways. Such relationships can be helpful in studying and understanding both the shape sequence and the related number sequence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.436,
            0.834,
            0.549
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The number of sides in the shape sequence of Regular Polygons is given by the counting numbers starting at 3, i.e., 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, .... That is why these shapes are called, respectively, "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "regular triangle",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "quadrilateral",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
